<!-- Placeholder only. Nitro's node-server preset builds its static-asset
     route table by scanning public/ during `vite build`, before
     scripts/generate-seo-files.mjs (a postbuild step) ever runs -- a file
     that doesn't exist here yet at that point gets no route at all, 404s
     forever even once the postbuild step writes the real one to
     .output/public/, regardless of content. This placeholder's only job is
     to exist at build time so Nitro registers the /sitemap.xml route; the
     postbuild step then overwrites this file in place with the real,
     tenant-aware sitemap index, which the server reads from disk on every
     request (confirmed via robots.txt, which follows the same pattern). -->
